{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Information.CountingModuliGrade","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qou_implies_p_neq_np_at_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qou_implies_p_neq_np_at_chi","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L107-L115","doc":"**The QOU-scoped separation at the derived residue.**  Specialises\n`qou_implies_p_neq_np` to the derived value $\\chi(A) = -6$: given a QOU (a\nhypothesis `QouPNeqNp decisionCost chiResidual`), the decision cost is not\npoly-bounded.  No non-vanishing hypothesis is needed — it is discharged by\n`chiResidual_ne_zero`.  **The `[QouPNeqNp …]` hypothesis is explicit**: this\ntheorem is genuinely conditional (no axiom, no auto-resolving instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.qou_implies_p_neq_np","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.qou_implies_p_neq_np","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L98-L105","doc":"**Given a QOU, P ≠ NP in that QOU (conditional; sorry-free from the\nhypotheses).**  Composes the faithfulness of a QOU instance with a\nnon-vanishing residue; the conclusion `PNeqNPInQOU decisionCost` is explicitly\nQOU-scoped — never an unconditional $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L96-L96","doc":"**Faithfulness (the open conjecture).**  *In the QOU*, a surviving\nobstruction residue forces the QOU-scoped decision separation (the decision\ncost is not poly-bounded).  This single implication is the irreducible\ncontent of `conj:qou-p-neq-np`; it needs a counting$\\to$decision transfer\nno known result supplies. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp.mk","kind":"ctor","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.QouPNeqNp","kind":"class","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L72-L96","doc":"**Conjecture (P ≠ NP in the QOU), §3b-cond carrier.**\n\n*Given a QOU* with substrate parameter\n$q_0 \\in \\mathbb{G}_m^{\\mathrm{nt}}(\\mathbb{R})$, the QOU decision-cost family\nis not polynomially bounded ([`PNeqNPInQOU decisionCost`]).  The statement is\n**conditional on the QOU**: an instance of this class is the hypothesis \"the\nQOU's obstruction faithfulness holds\", and only *from it* is the separation\nderived — never a bare $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$.\n\nNon-degenerate (§3b-tax): the class carries the **faithfulness implication**\n(a genuine sub-hypothesis — the counting→decision transfer), not the\nconclusion directly.  `residual` is a parameter (a `Prop`-class cannot hold\nℝ data); the QOU application fixes it to the derived `chiResidual`.\n\n**No instance is provided** — `faithful` is the open conjecture (the transfer\nno known result supplies), so downstream results carry `[QouPNeqNp …]`\nexplicitly. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:conj:qou-p-neq-np","label":"conj:qou-p-neq-np","md":"quantum-observable-universe/information-theory/qou-p-neq-np.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.chiResidual_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.chiResidual_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**Non-vanishing of the residue — derived, not conjectural\n(sorry-free).**  $\\chi(A) = -6 \\neq 0$; this leg of the conjecture\nis an axiom consequence, so the open content is entirely the\nfaithfulness (below). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.chiResidual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.chiResidual","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**The derived obstruction residue** $\\mathrm{res}_{\\mathcal{R}}(\\chi(A))$\nat the substrate.  The corpus derives the scalar value $\\chi(A) = -6$\n(`ex:chi-minus-six-derivation`, `prf:qou-obstruction-reduction`) with\nno computational-complexity input. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.PNeqNPInQOU","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.PNeqNPInQOU","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/QouPNeqNp.lean#L46-L57","doc":"**The QOU-scoped decision separation** — *the decision-cost family is not\npolynomially bounded*, `¬ FamilyPolyBounded decisionCost`.\n\nRead as \"$\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$ *in the QOU*\": no single `c·nᵏ`\ndominates the QOU decision cost at every moduli point.  This is the\nframework's own concrete, falsifiable separation — **not** an axiomatised\nliterature $\\mathrm{P}$/$\\mathrm{NP}$ (Mathlib has none; asserting one would\nlaunder, AGENTS.md §Axiomatization is NOT a Proof).  It is wired to the same\n`FamilyPolyBounded` predicate the *counting* axis proves super-poly\n(`physical_point_hard`); the open content is the counting→decision transfer\n(`QouPNeqNp.faithful`), never this target's meaning. ","signatureChunk":0}]}